  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "📝 Blog Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Blog names by topic, in the shapes that work: Crumbs & Butter, Notes from the Potting Shed, One More Chapter."
    },
    "intro": "A blog name has to say what you write about, sound like you, and still fit if your blog changes. This **blog name generator** has ideas for thirteen topics in the shapes good blog names usually take: two things and an ampersand, a place you write from, or a phrase that sounds like you.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Five shapes of blog name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>This &amp; that</strong>: two things you love, joined. <em>Lipstick &amp; Lattes</em>, <em>Crumbs &amp; Butter</em>.</li><li><strong>A place</strong>: where you write from. <em>Notes from the Potting Shed</em>, <em>The Little Pantry</em>.</li><li><strong>A phrase</strong>: something you'd actually say. <em>One More Chapter</em>, <em>Just One More Turn</em>.</li><li><strong>An honest adjective</strong>: <em>The Messy Kitchen Table</em> is more inviting than <em>The Perfect Kitchen</em>.</li><li><strong>Your own name</strong>: always available, and it grows with you. Worth considering if you might change topic.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Before you choose",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Check the domain and the handles.</strong> A name you can't get on the main social sites will cause trouble later.</li><li><strong>Don't box yourself in.</strong> A blog called <em>Vegan in Leeds</em> is stuck if you move or start eating cheese. A bit of room helps.</li><li><strong>Skip the year.</strong> Anything with 2026 in it will look old in 2027.</li><li><strong>Say it out loud.</strong> People will hear it in podcasts and conversation, so it needs to be easy to spell from hearing.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "A tiny history",
        "content": "<p>The word <em>weblog</em> was coined by Jorn Barger in 1997, for a page logging the web he'd read. In 1999 Peter Merholz split it, jokingly, into \"we blog\", and <em>blog</em> stuck. For other kinds of channel, try the <a href=\"podcast-name-generator.html\">Podcast Name Generator</a> or the <a href=\"youtube-channel-name-generator.html\">YouTube Channel Name Generator</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I choose a blog name?",
        "answer": "Pick the topic, generate a batch, and shortlist the ones that sound like you. Then check the domain and social handles are free, and say it aloud to make sure people can spell it."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these names for my blog?",
        "answer": "Yes, they're free to use and you don't need to credit the site. Many are everyday phrases, so search for the name first in case another blog already uses it."
      }
    ]
  }
}
